# Frontend UX Quality Bar

When creating or changing anything under `apps/web/`:

1. Read and follow the **Forms / Filters / Ant Design quality bar** in
   [`docs/technical/ui-requirements.md`](../../docs/technical/ui-requirements.md)
   (CHANGE-001 / US-042). Functional-but-bare screens are incomplete.
2. Every field: Azerbaijani label, placeholder, field-level validation
   (RHF + Zod + Ant `Form.Item`), correct input semantics. Decimal fields must
   block non-numeric typing (not only `inputMode`). Empty Selects use
   `undefined` so placeholders show.
3. Every list: usable FilterBar with **visible filter labels** (`FilterField`),
   search + status + domain filters, clear empty/loading/error/success,
   pagination with size changer, desktop table / mobile cards with all actions
   reachable.
4. Use Ant Design capabilities fully (`Select showSearch`, Modal confirm,
   Tag, Grid breakpoints, etc.). Prefer Ant Design **default theme** unless an
   Accepted ADR requires otherwise. Do not invent a parallel design system.
5. Never expose enum keys, API field names, or raw backend messages.
6. Backend-generated codes (ADR-024) are read-only and never submitted.
8. Soft-deactivate implies reactivate unless an Accepted Decision forbids it
   (see `operational-completeness.mdc`).
